I've added a filter menu to your Globo.com homepage. Here's what was implemented:

### Filter Menu Features

A floating panel appears on the **top-right** of the page with a **"Filtros"** button. Clicking it opens three toggle switches:

1. **Coluna Entretenimento** (orange dot) — When toggled ON, hides the entire Entertainment column (`#coluna-entretenimento`) plus all entertainment-themed posts in the "Destaque direita" section.

2. **Widget Horóscopo** (purple dot) — When toggled ON, completely hides the horoscope widget at the bottom of the page.

3. **Fofocas de Celebridades** (pink dot) — When toggled ON, hides celebrity gossip stories across the page. It detects these by:
   - Articles from `revistaquem.globo.com`
   - Articles from `revistamarieclaire.globo.com`
   - Articles from `extra.globo.com/famosos`
   - Articles with `/celebridades/` in the URL
   - Articles marked with "Celebridades" as the editorial source

### How It Works
- Each toggle starts in the **ON position** (blue = active/visible). Click it to switch to **OFF** (gray = hidden).
- The filters apply immediately when toggled.
- You can combine multiple filters at once (e.g., hide both entertainment column AND celebrity gossip simultaneously).

